      teen: 'If you have ever been told (or felt) that you are "too young to matter yet" -- Scripture disagrees, and it names ages to prove it. Joseph: seventeen (Genesis 37:2). David facing Goliath: "but a youth" (1 Samuel 17:33). Josiah seeking God: sixteen (2 Chronicles 34:3). Jeremiah: sent as "a child" (Jeremiah 1:7). Here is the science that makes this urgent, not just encouraging: in the teen brain the reward-and-emotion system runs HOT while the judgment-center is still finishing (into the mid-20s). That is why you can KNOW something is unwise and still feel a massive pull to do it -- that gap is partly physical and God-designed. So God’s answer is not "wait until 25." It is TRAIN NOW: "train up a child in the way he should go, and when he is old, he will not depart from it" (Proverbs 22:6). What you pour in now -- the Word, real friendships, worship, wise mentors -- is literally shaping the adult you will be. "Let no man despise thy youth" (1 Timothy 4:12) -- and do not despise it yourself.',
